---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';

const breadcrumbs = [{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Copyright & Takedown' }];
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Copyright and takedown"
  description="How to report a copyright issue and how we handle complaints, corrections, and removals."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
  updated="16 November 2026"
>
  <p>
    We respect copyright and publish original or properly licensed material. If you
    believe a page or file on this site infringes your rights, contact our grievance
    contact with the details below. We will review the complaint and remove or replace the
    material where appropriate.
  </p>

  <h2>Grievance contact</h2>
  <p>
    Grievance officer: <strong>TODO: name</strong>
    <br />
    Email: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.grievanceEmail}`}>{SITE.grievanceEmail}</a>
    <br />
    Response hours: Monday to Friday, 10:00–18:00 IST
  </p>
  <p class="text-sm text-stone-500">
    TODO: publish the grievance officer's name and a monitored contact before launch, as
    required for intermediaries under India's IT Rules, 2021.
  </p>

  <h2>What to include in a complaint</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your name, organisation, and contact details.</li>
    <li>The exact URL of the disputed page or file.</li>
    <li>A description of the work you own and the rights you believe are infringed.</li>
    <li>Proof of ownership or authority to act for the owner.</li>
    <li>A statement that you have a good-faith belief the use is unauthorised.</li>
    <li>A statement that the information in your notice is accurate.</li>
    <li>Your physical or electronic signature.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Do not include personal data about students, passwords, or result credentials. We do
    not need them to process a copyright complaint.
  </p>

  <h2>Timelines</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We aim to acknowledge a complete complaint within 24 hours.</li>
    <li>We aim to review and resolve complaints within 15 days.</li>
    <li>
      If we receive a valid court order or government direction, we will remove the
      material within 36 hours, subject to legal requirements.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What happens next</h2>
  <p>
    We may temporarily hide the material while we review it. If the complaint is valid, we
    remove or replace it and notify the contributor or reviewer. If the complaint is
    incomplete or disputed, we may ask for more information. We keep a record of
    complaints, actions, and dates.
  </p>

  <h2>Counter-response</h2>
  <p>
    If you submitted the material and believe the complaint is mistaken, send us your
    evidence, including the licence or written permission you rely on. We will review it
    before restoring anything.
  </p>

  <h2>Repeat infringement</h2>
  <p>We may restrict or remove contributors who repeatedly submit infringing material.</p>

  <h2>Our own content</h2>
  <p>
    If you want to reuse our original material, check the licence on the resource page. If
    no licence is stated, ask us in writing. Do not re-upload our PDFs as your own.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
